data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","sequence_number":891,"output_index":1,"item":{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_0c17af8fc60a9be3016adb516fef9081918fcbd34d9080d2e0","call_id":"call_c86bf4968cc043409e68e276ba8a489c","name":"check_draft","arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"base_input\":\"prior-candidate.json\",\"reset_base\":true,\"patches\":[{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/propositions/9/source/declaration\",\"value\":\"Real.volume_Icc\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/propositions/9/source/module\",\"value\":\"Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Lebesgue.Basic\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/1/text\",\"value\":\"For D>0 fix 0<s<D. Define C_a(A,δ) as the infimum of Nat-indexed δ-cover sums ∑'ᵢ ediam(Uᵢ)^a. Empty sets cost zero for a>0. Unfolding M008, its supremum over nonempty witnesses gives exactly the same term for nonempty cover members and zero for empty ones; thus M008 identifies Hausdorff measure with sup_{δ>0} C_a(A,δ), with no normalization. If δ₁≤δ₂, the δ₁-cover class is contained in the δ₂-cover class, so C_a(A,δ₁)≥C_a(A,δ₂); hence the decreasing-scale limit is this supremum. M001 yields C_s(E,δ)→∞ as δ↓0. For an arbitrary Nat-indexed δ-cover Vᵢ of F, put ρᵢ=ediam(Vᵢ), Aᵢ=π₁(Vᵢ), Bᵢ=π₂(Vᵢ). Projection is 1-Lipschitz, so both projected diameters are ≤ρᵢ. Choose ηᵢ=ε2^(−i−1)/(1+ρᵢ^s); since Bᵢ is bounded, enclose it in an open interval Jᵢ of length at most ρᵢ+ηᵢ by extending its infimum/supremum enclosure by total width ηᵢ. For each t∈[0,1] and x∈E, choose i with (x,t)∈Vᵢ; then x∈Aᵢ and t∈Bᵢ⊆Jᵢ. Thus the Aᵢ for which t∈Jᵢ cover E, and C_s(E,δ)≤∑'ᵢ 1_{Jᵢ∩[0,1]}(t)ρᵢ^s pointwise. Let ν=volume.restrict([0,1]). The set Jᵢ∩[0,1] is Borel, so its indicator times ρᵢ^s is measurable and AEMeasurable for ν. Also ν([0,1])=volume([0,1])=ofReal(1−0)=1 by M011, so ν is finite. Integrate the inequality using M009, then use M002; countability is ℕ and each summand is AEMeasurable. By M010 the i-th integral equals ρᵢ^sν(Jᵢ∩[0,1]). The restriction definition gives ν(S)=volume(S∩[0,1])≤volume(S) for measurable S. Enclose Jᵢ∩[0,1] in [aᵢ,bᵢ] with bᵢ−aᵢ≤ρᵢ+ηᵢ. Measure monotonicity (M013) gives volume(Jᵢ∩[0,1])≤volume([aᵢ,bᵢ]), and M011 evaluates the latter as ofReal(bᵢ−aᵢ)≤ofReal(ρᵢ+ηᵢ). Consequently C_s(E,δ)≤∑'ᵢρᵢ^(s+1)+∑'ᵢηᵢρᵢ^s≤∑'ᵢρᵢ^(s+1)+ε, since ∑ᵢ2^(−i−1)≤1. The cover is fixed and ε arbitrary; if its (s+1)-cost is finite, taking ε↓0 gives C_s(E,δ)≤that cost, while for infinite cost the inequality is immediate. Taking the infimum over all δ-covers yields C_s(E,δ)≤C_(s+1)(F,δ). The left tends to infinity as δ↓0, so the right does too; M008 then gives H^(s+1)(F)=∞. M001 at the NNReal coercion of s+1 gives s+1≤dim_H(F). As this holds for every 0<s<D, density yields D+1≤dim_H(F).\"}]}}","status":"completed"}}

